WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:03.759
Hi, welcome back to
Nagarjuna number three.

00:00:03.759 --> 00:00:07.740
We've reached now Chapter 14.

00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:10.347
And this is called PHRAD PA BRTAG PA

00:00:10.347 --> 00:00:12.000
PHRAD PA BRTAG PA

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:13.285
You guys know BRTAG PA

00:00:13.285 --> 00:00:16.088
because that's 'pariksha'.

00:00:16.088 --> 00:00:16.921
Pariksha means

00:00:16.921 --> 00:00:20.230
'an investigation', so
each of these chapters

00:00:20.230 --> 00:00:21.630
is a separate investigation.

00:00:21.630 --> 00:00:24.200
It's like Nagarjuna's the police

00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:28.170
or a detective and he's
investigating different people,

00:00:28.170 --> 00:00:29.580
different things in the universe,

00:00:29.580 --> 00:00:32.950
and this one is called PHRAD PA BRTAG PA.

00:00:32.950 --> 00:00:37.106
He's investigating can
something touch something else?

00:00:37.106 --> 00:00:38.570
PHRAD PA, can something

00:00:38.570 --> 00:00:41.403
make contact with something else?

00:00:41.403 --> 00:00:43.810
We've been talking about it all along,

00:00:43.810 --> 00:00:46.900
but here's a whole chapter dedicated to:

00:00:46.900 --> 00:00:50.000
can something touch something else?

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:53.060
By the way, if it cannot
touch something else,

00:00:53.060 --> 00:00:57.440
then that draws into
question causation itself.

00:00:57.440 --> 00:01:02.440
If you put gas in a car, but
the engine can't touch the gas,

00:01:02.440 --> 00:01:05.770
then what's making the car go?

00:01:05.770 --> 00:01:08.120
Okay?

00:01:08.120 --> 00:01:12.759
Here we go with the first verse.

00:01:12.759 --> 00:01:16.530
We know that we have to watch out for

00:01:16.530 --> 00:01:20.300
possible... this might be the other guy,

00:01:20.300 --> 00:01:22.317
but I'm going to make it easy for you

00:01:22.317 --> 00:01:25.420
and tell you the first verse here is us.

00:01:25.420 --> 00:01:28.220
The first two verses is us.

00:01:28.220 --> 00:01:31.770
So here we go.

00:01:31.770 --> 00:01:36.496
BLTA BYA LTA BA LTA BA PO

00:01:36.496 --> 00:01:37.329
[Sneezes]

00:01:37.329 --> 00:01:41.232
Is there any contact between
my nose and the tissue paper?

00:01:41.232 --> 00:01:42.341
[students Llughing]

00:01:42.341 --> 00:01:43.716
,BLTA BYA LTA BA LTA BA PO,

00:01:43.716 --> 00:01:45.690
,GSUM PO DE DAG GNYIS GNYIS DANG,

00:01:45.690 --> 00:01:47.590
,THAMS CAD KYANG NI PHAN TSUN DU,

00:01:47.590 --> 00:01:50.224
,PHRAD PAR 'GYUR PA YOD MA YIN,

00:01:50.224 --> 00:01:52.200
So he's going to discuss

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:55.290
a kind of a difficult kind of touching.

00:01:55.290 --> 00:01:59.511
When I look at Rebecca, right now,

00:01:59.511 --> 00:02:01.950
I have... Rebecca is the BLTA BYA,

00:02:01.950 --> 00:02:06.914
the 'lookee', the thing I'm looking at.

00:02:06.914 --> 00:02:09.474
LTA BA means 'the looking'

00:02:09.474 --> 00:02:12.498
and LTA BA PO is me, the 'looker'.

00:02:12.498 --> 00:02:15.778
Those three. Do they ever make contact?

00:02:15.778 --> 00:02:18.200
What kind of contact, Geshe-la?

00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:23.121
Do these two, do these
two, or do these two

00:02:23.121 --> 00:02:24.321
to make contact,

00:02:24.321 --> 00:02:26.337
which means GNYIS GNYIS DANG,

00:02:26.337 --> 00:02:28.070
do they make dual contact?

00:02:28.070 --> 00:02:30.540
Or THAMS CAD KYANG NI PHAN TSUN DU

00:02:30.540 --> 00:02:32.700
means do the three ever touch each other?

00:02:32.700 --> 00:02:36.306
So we got some different
possibilities, right?

00:02:36.306 --> 00:02:39.830
Geshe-la,'looker';
Rebecca being 'looked at';

00:02:39.830 --> 00:02:42.030
and then the verb 'of looking' -

00:02:42.030 --> 00:02:44.230
do those there ever touch each other?

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:45.810
And do any two touch each other?

00:02:45.810 --> 00:02:48.330
Does Geshe-la touch the looking?

00:02:48.330 --> 00:02:51.233
Or does the looking touch Rebecca?

00:02:51.233 --> 00:02:54.420
Or does the... Geshe-la
touch Rebecca somehow?

00:02:54.420 --> 00:02:57.890
Is there any touch going
on between those three,

00:02:57.890 --> 00:03:01.176
any combination of touching?

00:03:01.176 --> 00:03:02.589
,DE BZHIN 'DOD CHAGS CHAGS PA DANG,

00:03:02.589 --> 00:03:04.614
,CHAGS PAR BYA BA

00:03:04.614 --> 00:03:07.880
And then let's take it to
your negative emotions,

00:03:07.880 --> 00:03:11.070
which is a big part of
Buddhist practice, right?

00:03:11.070 --> 00:03:14.270
When you want something bad enough

00:03:14.270 --> 00:03:17.470
to hurt somebody to get it,

00:03:17.470 --> 00:03:21.692
then there's the 'wanter',
there's 'the wanting',

00:03:21.692 --> 00:03:23.640
and there's 'the thing you want'.

00:03:23.640 --> 00:03:24.840
Do they ever touch?

00:03:24.840 --> 00:03:27.440
Or do any combination of
them touch each other?

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:32.120
So he starts out with something
innocuous, like looking,

00:03:32.120 --> 00:03:36.040
and then he's going to take
it to negative emotions:

00:03:36.040 --> 00:03:40.170
hating somebody or wanting something

00:03:40.170 --> 00:03:43.484
bad enough to steal it.

00:03:43.484 --> 00:03:46.095
CHAGS PAR BYA BA, and then he says...

00:03:46.095 --> 00:03:48.410
By the way, you have
to read over the verse,

00:03:48.410 --> 00:03:51.452
over the lines here, or you won't get it.

00:03:51.452 --> 00:03:52.285
NYON MONGS PA, LHAG MA

00:03:52.285 --> 00:03:55.902
NYON MONGS PA, LHAG MA

00:03:55.902 --> 00:03:57.610
Which means and then let's talk about

00:03:57.610 --> 00:03:59.510
all the other mental afflictions.

00:03:59.510 --> 00:04:00.970
We got desire covered here:

00:04:00.970 --> 00:04:05.180
'desirer', 'desiree', and the 'desiring'.

00:04:05.180 --> 00:04:06.800
And then he says... and then you have to

00:04:06.800 --> 00:04:08.300
read across the lines,

00:04:08.300 --> 00:04:10.699
NYON MONGS PA, LHAG MA

00:04:10.699 --> 00:04:11.540
The rest of these,

00:04:11.540 --> 00:04:13.315
DANG SKYE MCHED KYI LHAG MA

00:04:13.315 --> 00:04:14.271
Then let's... By the way,

00:04:14.271 --> 00:04:16.710
SKYE MCHED means in Abhidharma.

00:04:16.710 --> 00:04:18.960
Here it means 'the senses'.

00:04:18.960 --> 00:04:19.793
So we talked about seeing,

00:04:19.793 --> 00:04:21.526
but what about hearing,

00:04:21.526 --> 00:04:24.310
what about smelling, what about tasting,

00:04:24.310 --> 00:04:26.520
what about feeling?

00:04:26.520 --> 00:04:30.680
Does the feeler ever touch the...

00:04:30.680 --> 00:04:32.300
Does the feeler ever touch

00:04:32.300 --> 00:04:35.100
the object that they're feeling?

00:04:35.100 --> 00:04:37.842
And does your jealousy ever touch

00:04:37.842 --> 00:04:40.660
what you're jealous about?

00:04:40.660 --> 00:04:44.492
So let's talk about all those things.

00:04:44.492 --> 00:04:48.023
I have a picture here of a lady.

00:04:48.023 --> 00:04:52.273
When you want money,

00:04:52.273 --> 00:04:55.273
and then I keep saying,

00:04:55.273 --> 00:04:57.780
enough to hurt someone to get it,

00:04:57.780 --> 00:04:59.680
I say you cannot touch the money.

00:04:59.680 --> 00:05:04.050
When you want money bad enough

00:05:04.050 --> 00:05:06.760
that you will hurt someone else,

00:05:06.760 --> 00:05:09.100
I say you cannot touch the money.

00:05:09.100 --> 00:05:11.280
You never touch the money.

00:05:11.280 --> 00:05:16.270
So that's a... you've
got to think about it.

00:05:16.270 --> 00:05:19.460
Can you touch money if
you want to give it away?

00:05:19.460 --> 00:05:21.778
Yes.

00:05:21.778 --> 00:05:23.390
Maybe.

00:05:23.390 --> 00:05:25.405
Can you touch money if
you want to steal it?

00:05:25.405 --> 00:05:27.496
Never.

00:05:27.496 --> 00:05:29.100
All right.

00:05:29.100 --> 00:05:31.882
We're going to learn some
Sanskrit here right away.

00:05:31.882 --> 00:05:33.030
'sansarga'

00:05:33.030 --> 00:05:36.550
This is not Sansara.

00:05:36.550 --> 00:05:39.260
It's Sansarga.

00:05:39.260 --> 00:05:43.668
This means 'touching', making contact.

00:05:43.668 --> 00:05:48.668
It has two parts, 'san-',
or 'sam-', and 'sarga'.

00:05:48.940 --> 00:05:53.200
By itself, sam, when in combination with S

00:05:53.200 --> 00:05:54.530
it changes to S-A-N.

00:05:54.530 --> 00:05:59.450
The pronunciation
changes to san, sansarga.

00:05:59.450 --> 00:06:04.434
So san- means 'together',
it comes from 'sam',

00:06:04.434 --> 00:06:09.393
that changes the C-O, like
'committee' or 'convention',

00:06:09.393 --> 00:06:12.000
coming together or meeting together,

00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:14.550
sending together, committee.

00:06:14.550 --> 00:06:16.980
So the 'com' is easy, the C-O-M is easy.

00:06:16.980 --> 00:06:18.660
What's the 'sarga'?

00:06:18.660 --> 00:06:22.520
It comes from √sṛj,
which is a Sanskrit root,

00:06:22.520 --> 00:06:24.430
and that means 'to move together'

00:06:24.430 --> 00:06:27.100
or 'to move towards each other'.

00:06:27.100 --> 00:06:31.689
And to surge, we have that
verb in English, sansarga.

00:06:31.689 --> 00:06:34.820
In Indo-European, which is also

00:06:34.820 --> 00:06:38.670
a kind of an ancient Sanskrit, S drops out

00:06:38.670 --> 00:06:43.580
and this √sṛj becomes √reg,
and it means 'to regulate'

00:06:43.580 --> 00:06:48.580
or 'to reign over something'
or to... or the right way.

00:06:48.750 --> 00:06:51.470
So it means 'straight',
'to move straight'.

00:06:51.470 --> 00:06:54.840
By itself, surge means 'to move towards',

00:06:54.840 --> 00:06:56.880
san- means 'the two things move together'

00:06:56.880 --> 00:06:58.040
and they touch.

00:06:58.040 --> 00:07:01.479
So that's sansarga.

00:07:01.479 --> 00:07:04.046
Is it possible that things ever

00:07:04.046 --> 00:07:07.720
surge towards each other?

00:07:07.720 --> 00:07:11.369
Sansarga. Yes or no? Here we go.

00:07:11.369 --> 00:07:16.334
All right, next verse.

00:07:16.334 --> 00:07:20.426
,GZHAN DANG GZHAN DU PHRAD 'GYUR NA,

00:07:20.426 --> 00:07:24.491
,GANG PHYIR BLTA BYA LA SOGS LA,

00:07:24.491 --> 00:07:26.683
,GZHAN DE YOD PA MA YIN PA,

00:07:26.683 --> 00:07:29.341
,DE PHYIR PHRAD PAR MI 'GYUR RO,

00:07:29.341 --> 00:07:32.242
Now here's our comment on touching.

00:07:32.242 --> 00:07:34.790
GZHAN DANG GZHAN DU PHRAD 'GYUR NA

00:07:34.790 --> 00:07:39.090
If two things which are
different from each other

00:07:39.090 --> 00:07:41.282
can touch each other,

00:07:41.282 --> 00:07:45.166
GANG PHYIR BLTA BYA LA SOGS LA,

00:07:45.166 --> 00:07:50.166
GZHAN DE YOD PA MA YIN PA

00:07:50.181 --> 00:07:52.581
I'm asking you,

00:07:52.581 --> 00:07:55.205
can your eye touch your seeing?

00:07:55.205 --> 00:07:59.421
Can your eye, can the 'seer'

00:07:59.421 --> 00:08:02.428
make contact with the 'seeing'?

00:08:02.428 --> 00:08:05.513
If not, the seer cannot see.

00:08:05.513 --> 00:08:09.200
If the seer cannot touch the seeing,

00:08:09.200 --> 00:08:12.180
if the seer never makes
contact with the seeing,

00:08:12.180 --> 00:08:14.870
then they must be smelling, for example.

00:08:14.870 --> 00:08:15.703
So do they ever make contact?

00:08:15.703 --> 00:08:19.102
Yes.

00:08:19.102 --> 00:08:23.267
Does seer, the eye, ever touch the seeing?

00:08:23.267 --> 00:08:24.820
They have to.

00:08:24.820 --> 00:08:26.980
Does the seeing ever touch Rebecca?

00:08:26.980 --> 00:08:28.536
It has too.

00:08:28.536 --> 00:08:29.750
PHRAD 'GYUR NA

00:08:29.750 --> 00:08:33.740
But if they touch, GZHAN DE YOD PA MA YIN

00:08:33.740 --> 00:08:34.920
then they have to be separate,

00:08:34.920 --> 00:08:38.578
and if they're separate, they don't exist.

00:08:38.578 --> 00:08:42.430
Or there's no such thing as other,

00:08:42.430 --> 00:08:47.320
that Geshe-la cannot be
different from Rebecca

00:08:47.320 --> 00:08:51.620
if Geshe-la can see Rebecca.

00:08:51.620 --> 00:08:53.417
They cannot be different.

00:08:53.417 --> 00:08:54.940
DE PHYIR PHRAD PAR MI 'GYUR RO

00:08:54.940 --> 00:08:56.840
Therefore, there is no sansarga.

00:08:56.840 --> 00:08:58.707
What does that mean?

00:08:58.707 --> 00:08:59.650
Things never touch each other.

00:08:59.650 --> 00:09:01.670
Things never contact each other.

00:09:01.670 --> 00:09:04.111
When I open my eyes,

00:09:04.111 --> 00:09:05.936
it's not the opening my eyes

00:09:05.936 --> 00:09:09.170
that makes me see Rebecca.

00:09:09.170 --> 00:09:10.920
Something else has happened.

00:09:10.920 --> 00:09:13.185
What's happening?

00:09:13.185 --> 00:09:15.047
Seeds are opening in Geshe-la's mind

00:09:15.047 --> 00:09:16.940
and Geshe-la sees Rebecca.

00:09:16.940 --> 00:09:19.381
In the Mind-Only School,

00:09:19.381 --> 00:09:21.914
she's never outside of my mind.

00:09:21.914 --> 00:09:24.480
I'm just watching pictures in my own mind.

00:09:24.480 --> 00:09:27.610
But in the higher
schools, she is out there,

00:09:27.610 --> 00:09:29.570
she is a separate person,

00:09:29.570 --> 00:09:34.537
but the reason I see
her as separate from me

00:09:34.537 --> 00:09:37.200
is that seeds are opening in my mind

00:09:37.200 --> 00:09:39.370
for me to see her as separate from me.

00:09:39.370 --> 00:09:42.160
And it's not that my eye is seeing her.

00:09:42.160 --> 00:09:47.125
It's not in my eye is making contact.

00:09:47.125 --> 00:09:51.220
The theme of my next picture is

00:09:51.220 --> 00:09:53.948
things that don't exist
cannot touch each other.

00:09:53.948 --> 00:09:58.948
A self-existent eye could not
touch self-existent seeing

00:09:58.948 --> 00:10:01.700
to reach a self-existent Rebecca.

00:10:01.700 --> 00:10:05.020
It's not... you can't have contact,

00:10:05.020 --> 00:10:06.960
you can't have a war between

00:10:06.960 --> 00:10:09.360
these two rabbits with horns.

00:10:09.360 --> 00:10:11.720
And this is the classic Buddhist example

00:10:11.720 --> 00:10:15.163
of something that's impossible.

00:10:15.163 --> 00:10:20.085
They call it a 'jackalope' in the West.

00:10:20.085 --> 00:10:22.590
Jack-rabbit-antelope or something.

00:10:22.590 --> 00:10:26.200
So try to imagine two
things that don't exist

00:10:26.200 --> 00:10:30.517
touching each other,  and
you've got the right picture.

00:10:30.517 --> 00:10:34.160
All right, next verse.

00:10:34.160 --> 00:10:37.363
,BLTA BYA LA SOGS 'BA' ZHIG LA,

00:10:37.363 --> 00:10:39.712
,GZHAN NYID MED PAR MA ZAD KYI,

00:10:39.712 --> 00:10:42.742
Let's start with that, because
it's already difficult.

00:10:42.742 --> 00:10:44.850
BLTA BYA LA SOGS

00:10:44.850 --> 00:10:46.890
Now we had three elements in the act

00:10:46.890 --> 00:10:48.800
of Geshe-la seeing Rebecca:

00:10:48.800 --> 00:10:51.510
there was the 'see-ee', which is Rebecca;

00:10:51.510 --> 00:10:53.760
there's the 'seer' which is Geshe-la;

00:10:53.760 --> 00:10:56.870
and then there's the
'seeing' between them.

00:10:56.870 --> 00:10:59.240
Now let's take them individually.

00:10:59.240 --> 00:11:01.610
He says 'BA' ZHIG.

00:11:01.610 --> 00:11:05.770
Let's just take Rebecca without the seeing

00:11:05.770 --> 00:11:07.693
and without Geshe-la looking.

00:11:07.693 --> 00:11:10.100
GZHAN NYID MED PAR MA ZAD KYI

00:11:10.100 --> 00:11:14.041
She cannot be considered

00:11:14.041 --> 00:11:19.039
separate because she's alone.

00:11:19.039 --> 00:11:23.143
Got it? That's a little tricky.

00:11:23.143 --> 00:11:26.300
Let's forget Geshe-la. Forget the looking.

00:11:26.300 --> 00:11:28.830
Let's just talk about Rebecca.

00:11:28.830 --> 00:11:33.602
Now, what kind of relationships
have we got there?

00:11:33.602 --> 00:11:37.880
Well, zero, because
something has to be different

00:11:37.880 --> 00:11:39.860
to have a relationship.

00:11:39.860 --> 00:11:44.030
A person can't have relationship

00:11:44.030 --> 00:11:48.560
with exactly the same person,
because there's only one.

00:11:48.560 --> 00:11:50.000
So eliminate that one.

00:11:50.000 --> 00:11:51.600
Nagarjuna says that one's easy.

00:11:51.600 --> 00:11:54.930
Take one of the three elements of seeing -

00:11:54.930 --> 00:11:59.872
seer, seeing, and seen -
and just treat one of them:

00:11:59.872 --> 00:12:01.940
'BA' ZHIG, seen,

00:12:01.940 --> 00:12:03.130
can it have a relationship?

00:12:03.130 --> 00:12:05.270
No, we don't have to talk about that one.

00:12:05.270 --> 00:12:08.430
Well let's talk ,GANG YANG
GANG DANG LHAN CIG TU,

00:12:08.430 --> 00:12:11.870
Let's talk about two of them
sitting in the same room:

00:12:11.870 --> 00:12:13.990
Geshe-la and Rebecca.

00:12:13.990 --> 00:12:18.487
,GZHAN PA NYID DU MI 'THAD DO, well then

00:12:18.487 --> 00:12:22.096
they couldn't be something else.

00:12:22.096 --> 00:12:26.171
They can't be something else
if they're only one thing.

00:12:26.171 --> 00:12:30.620
And they can't be something
else if they're not one thing.

00:12:30.620 --> 00:12:32.384
That's Nagarjuna.

00:12:32.384 --> 00:12:35.653
If they're not one thing,
they can't be something else

00:12:35.653 --> 00:12:39.220
because to you something
else means out there,

00:12:39.220 --> 00:12:40.700
from it's own side.

00:12:40.700 --> 00:12:41.994
That's all.

00:12:41.994 --> 00:12:45.117
You got to keep remembering that.

00:12:45.117 --> 00:12:47.925
For some reason, I thought it was

00:12:47.925 --> 00:12:51.974
really clever to have a cherry

00:12:51.974 --> 00:12:54.699
that was itself

00:12:54.699 --> 00:12:57.607
but something else at the same time.

00:12:57.607 --> 00:13:00.241
[Laughing]

00:13:00.241 --> 00:13:05.118
Look, it's hard to find
picture like that [laughs].

00:13:05.118 --> 00:13:08.432
All right, nevermind.

00:13:08.432 --> 00:13:10.330
Well, I'm not going to say a bad word.

00:13:10.330 --> 00:13:12.800
All right.

00:13:12.800 --> 00:13:16.340
You are witness, I do
have some self control.

00:13:16.340 --> 00:13:21.193
Okay, next verse.

00:13:21.193 --> 00:13:24.367
,GZHAN NI GZHAN LA BRTEN TE GZHAN,

00:13:24.367 --> 00:13:27.200
,GZHAN MED PAR GZHAN GZHAN MI 'GYUR,

00:13:27.200 --> 00:13:28.833
,GANG LA BRTEN TE GANG YIN PA,

00:13:28.833 --> 00:13:30.925
,DE NI DE LAS GZHAN MI 'THAD,

00:13:30.925 --> 00:13:34.171
This is very difficult, let's
go through line by line.

00:13:34.171 --> 00:13:37.040
GZHAN NI GZHAN LA BRTEN TE GZHAN

00:13:37.040 --> 00:13:40.761
Others are others relative to others.

00:13:40.761 --> 00:13:42.940
Others are others relative to others.

00:13:42.940 --> 00:13:43.960
That's okay.

00:13:43.960 --> 00:13:47.010
Others are others relative to others.

00:13:47.010 --> 00:13:50.303
And he uses the classical example

00:13:50.303 --> 00:13:55.243
of a water vase and a bolt of cloth.

00:13:55.243 --> 00:13:58.718
You could say a car and a refrigerator.

00:13:58.718 --> 00:14:00.660
Let's use that.

00:14:00.660 --> 00:14:05.040
When you say a car is
different from a refrigerator,

00:14:05.040 --> 00:14:09.980
the difference is drawn by
observing both together.

00:14:09.980 --> 00:14:14.136
A car can only be different
from a refrigerator

00:14:14.136 --> 00:14:16.907
if you see the other thing that's there

00:14:16.907 --> 00:14:19.102
before you decide it's different.

00:14:19.102 --> 00:14:22.166
You've got to have two things there.

00:14:22.166 --> 00:14:25.751
GZHAN MED PAR GZHAN GZHAN MI 'GYUR

00:14:25.751 --> 00:14:27.710
If there was no car,

00:14:27.710 --> 00:14:32.668
you couldn't call the
refrigerator different from... ?

00:14:32.668 --> 00:14:35.286
There has to be something else there.

00:14:35.286 --> 00:14:37.610
GANG LA BRTEN TE GANG YIN PA

00:14:37.610 --> 00:14:41.693
Anything that is something
relative to something else,

00:14:41.693 --> 00:14:43.667
DE NI DE LAS GZHAN MI 'THAD

00:14:43.667 --> 00:14:48.625
Could never be other than it.

00:14:48.625 --> 00:14:53.562
Nothing which is different from
something else by comparison

00:14:53.562 --> 00:14:57.020
could be called something else,

00:14:57.020 --> 00:14:59.370
self-existently.

00:14:59.370 --> 00:15:02.630
Nothing which is something
else by comparison,

00:15:02.630 --> 00:15:05.120
a refrigerator is different from a car,

00:15:05.120 --> 00:15:10.113
but it cannot be called
different in and of itself.

00:15:10.113 --> 00:15:14.053
Once you get into dependence,
even if you're not speaking

00:15:14.053 --> 00:15:16.280
about dependence on mental seeds,

00:15:16.280 --> 00:15:18.550
you're already messing with

00:15:18.550 --> 00:15:20.990
the fact that something
could be self-existent.

00:15:20.990 --> 00:15:24.210
Once you say something
depends on something else,

00:15:24.210 --> 00:15:26.220
you've already almost left

00:15:26.220 --> 00:15:28.900
the realm of self-existence.

00:15:28.900 --> 00:15:33.790
The word 'dependent origination',
or occurring in reliance.

00:15:33.790 --> 00:15:35.629
Once you get into comparison

00:15:35.629 --> 00:15:38.220
or one thing depending on another,

00:15:38.220 --> 00:15:40.600
it's difficult to start asserting that

00:15:40.600 --> 00:15:42.870
they are both self-existent,

00:15:42.870 --> 00:15:46.460
and they exist in and of themselves.

00:15:46.460 --> 00:15:48.576
All right.

00:15:48.576 --> 00:15:53.506
No one is tall where tall
and short are compared.

00:15:53.506 --> 00:15:58.485
Okay.

00:15:58.485 --> 00:16:03.460
So this is a little tricky.

00:16:03.460 --> 00:16:07.025
Normally, you've got that picture?

00:16:07.025 --> 00:16:09.980
Normally you would say the young girl

00:16:09.980 --> 00:16:13.340
is short by comparison to
her mother or her sister,

00:16:13.340 --> 00:16:15.600
I don't know who it is, her mom I guess.

00:16:15.600 --> 00:16:16.510
Normally you would say

00:16:16.510 --> 00:16:20.270
she's short compared to her mom.

00:16:20.270 --> 00:16:24.093
Normally you would say that.

00:16:24.093 --> 00:16:29.043
And Nagarjuna says if the mom is tall...

00:16:29.043 --> 00:16:31.330
If you can only call the mom tall

00:16:31.330 --> 00:16:36.178
by comparison to her
daughter, then she's not tall.

00:16:36.178 --> 00:16:39.180
I'll say it again. If you
can only call the mom tall

00:16:39.180 --> 00:16:41.530
by comparison to her short daughter,

00:16:41.530 --> 00:16:45.150
then we can't really say the mom is tall.

00:16:45.150 --> 00:16:45.983
Got it?

00:16:45.983 --> 00:16:48.230
'Really say' means in and of herself,

00:16:48.230 --> 00:16:49.820
meaning self-existently.

00:16:49.820 --> 00:16:51.520
Is she tall?

00:16:51.520 --> 00:16:52.910
I don't know.

00:16:52.910 --> 00:16:54.280
Is she tall compared to her daughter?

00:16:54.280 --> 00:16:55.113
Yes.

00:16:55.113 --> 00:16:57.521
Then she's not tall.

00:16:57.521 --> 00:16:59.550
If she's only tall with
reference to something else,

00:16:59.550 --> 00:17:02.810
then she's not tall in herself.

00:17:02.810 --> 00:17:03.643
Got it?

00:17:03.643 --> 00:17:05.745
That's easy, right?

00:17:05.745 --> 00:17:07.591
We understood one verse, all right.

00:17:07.591 --> 00:17:09.972
[students Laughing]

00:17:09.972 --> 00:17:14.904
Where are you going after that, Nagarjuna?

00:17:14.904 --> 00:17:18.004
,GAL TE GZHAN NI GZHAN LAS GZHAN,

00:17:18.004 --> 00:17:20.346
,DE TSE GZHAN MED PAR GZHAN 'GYUR,

00:17:20.346 --> 00:17:22.429
,GZHAN MED PAR NI GZHAN 'GYUR PA,

00:17:22.429 --> 00:17:25.712
,YOD MIN DE YI PHYIR NA MED,

00:17:25.712 --> 00:17:30.610
GAL TE GZHAN NI GZHAN LAS GZHAN

00:17:30.610 --> 00:17:35.271
if a car is self-existently
different from a refrigerator,

00:17:35.271 --> 00:17:38.146
DE TSE GZHAN MED PAR GZHAN 'GYUR

00:17:38.146 --> 00:17:40.363
in that case something which

00:17:40.363 --> 00:17:42.952
is not different became different.

00:17:42.952 --> 00:17:45.960
If a car is only a car
relative to a refrigerator,

00:17:45.960 --> 00:17:50.937
then a car, which was
different, is not different.

00:17:50.937 --> 00:17:54.166
GZHAN MED PAR NI GZHAN 'GYUR PA

00:17:54.166 --> 00:17:56.840
GZHAN MED PAR here means

00:17:56.840 --> 00:18:01.130
'that which doesn't have another'.

00:18:01.130 --> 00:18:02.720
That which doesn't have another,

00:18:02.720 --> 00:18:06.090
meaning the mom by herself.

00:18:06.090 --> 00:18:08.043
The tall mom by herself.

00:18:08.043 --> 00:18:11.660
GZHAN MED PAR NI GZHAN 'GYUR PA

00:18:11.660 --> 00:18:14.859
If the mom were tall,

00:18:14.859 --> 00:18:18.325
GZHAN MED PAR

00:18:18.325 --> 00:18:20.687
without the girl around,

00:18:20.687 --> 00:18:24.928
YOD MIN DE YI PHYIR NA MED

00:18:24.928 --> 00:18:26.300
then she wouldn't be tall.

00:18:26.300 --> 00:18:29.930
If the mom were tall by
comparison to the daughter,

00:18:29.930 --> 00:18:33.550
she wouldn't be tall because
she's not tall by herself.

00:18:33.550 --> 00:18:37.857
She's only tall by comparison.

00:18:37.857 --> 00:18:39.330
All right.

00:18:39.330 --> 00:18:43.188
All right.

00:18:43.188 --> 00:18:48.140
A coffee cup is not different
from a pair of jeans.

00:18:48.140 --> 00:18:53.085
I was trying to find a... I
was trying to get this lady,

00:18:53.085 --> 00:18:55.220
I was trying to find a lady drinking,

00:18:55.220 --> 00:18:59.465
somebody drinking coffee with jeans on.

00:18:59.465 --> 00:19:02.628
Is the coffee cup the jeans?

00:19:02.628 --> 00:19:03.660
No.

00:19:03.660 --> 00:19:08.340
Is the coffee cup
different from the jeans?

00:19:08.340 --> 00:19:10.650
- [Student] Only if the jeans are there.

00:19:10.650 --> 00:19:12.340
- Yeah, only if the jeans are there,

00:19:12.340 --> 00:19:16.191
which means it's not different by itself.

00:19:16.191 --> 00:19:17.570
It's not really different,

00:19:17.570 --> 00:19:20.300
because it's only different by comparison.

00:19:20.300 --> 00:19:23.278
Is coffee different from jeans?

00:19:23.278 --> 00:19:24.640
- [Student] Yes.
- Yeah.

00:19:24.640 --> 00:19:25.720
Why?

00:19:25.720 --> 00:19:27.950
Because when you look at the coffee cup

00:19:27.950 --> 00:19:30.522
you see it doesn't look
like the jeans, right?

00:19:30.522 --> 00:19:33.420
Then that difference is
dependent on something else,

00:19:33.420 --> 00:19:37.135
and it's not part of the coffee cup.

00:19:37.135 --> 00:19:38.910
Okay?

00:19:38.910 --> 00:19:41.560
All right.

00:19:41.560 --> 00:19:46.543
Somewhere it applies to
racism in there I think.

00:19:46.543 --> 00:19:49.695
Next verse.

00:19:49.695 --> 00:19:52.586
,GZHAN NYID GZHAN LA YOD MA YIN,

00:19:52.586 --> 00:19:54.944
,GZHAN MA YIN LA'ANG YOD MA YIN,

00:19:54.944 --> 00:19:56.761
,GZHAN NYID YOD PA MA YIN NA,

00:19:56.761 --> 00:19:58.923
,GZHAN NAM DE NYID YOD MA YIN,

00:19:58.923 --> 00:20:01.497
GZHAN NYID GZHAN LA YOD MA YIN

00:20:01.497 --> 00:20:02.389
Being something other

00:20:02.389 --> 00:20:06.652
is not part of anything which is other.

00:20:06.652 --> 00:20:11.441
Being other is not part of being other.

00:20:11.441 --> 00:20:14.815
Being other is not part
of something other.

00:20:14.815 --> 00:20:16.665
GZHAN MA YIN LA'ANG YOD MA YIN

00:20:16.665 --> 00:20:21.660
Neither is that other not an other.

00:20:21.660 --> 00:20:26.060
GZHAN NYID YOD PA MA YIN NA

00:20:26.060 --> 00:20:29.326
If there is no other,

00:20:29.326 --> 00:20:31.934
which is general otherness -

00:20:31.934 --> 00:20:32.767
otherness as a concept -

00:20:32.767 --> 00:20:34.900
GZHAN NYID

00:20:34.900 --> 00:20:39.889
is being treated as otherness.

00:20:39.889 --> 00:20:43.637
If there's no such thing as otherness,

00:20:43.637 --> 00:20:47.538
then there's no other, and other

00:20:47.538 --> 00:20:52.522
in the sense of being one
and the same by comparison.

00:20:52.522 --> 00:20:57.223
If there is no otherness by itself,

00:20:57.223 --> 00:21:01.321
then there can't be
otherness by comparison.

00:21:01.321 --> 00:21:03.940
If there's no concept of otherness,

00:21:03.940 --> 00:21:06.670
then you can't have
otherness by comparison,

00:21:06.670 --> 00:21:10.590
because that's what the concept
of otherness applies to,

00:21:10.590 --> 00:21:13.440
is otherness by comparison.

00:21:13.440 --> 00:21:16.650
If otherness by comparison were real,

00:21:16.650 --> 00:21:21.635
it wouldn't need to be
compared with something else.

00:21:21.635 --> 00:21:24.840
If something's only something

00:21:24.840 --> 00:21:27.100
by comparison with something else,

00:21:27.100 --> 00:21:29.370
then it's not really that thing.

00:21:29.370 --> 00:21:32.420
It's partly the other thing.

00:21:32.420 --> 00:21:37.420
So therefore the idea of
otherness is questionable.

00:21:41.886 --> 00:21:46.853
(thinking)

00:21:46.853 --> 00:21:51.718
Got a picture here.

00:21:51.718 --> 00:21:55.896
Are they other or are they the same?

00:21:55.896 --> 00:21:59.204
Huh?

00:21:59.204 --> 00:22:03.587
Are they other or are they the same?

00:22:03.587 --> 00:22:04.634
What? huh?

00:22:04.634 --> 00:22:06.993
- [Student] Who's asking?
What's the picture of?

00:22:06.993 --> 00:22:09.859
- It's a duck with a goose and a chicken.

00:22:09.859 --> 00:22:14.134
Are they other or are they the same?

00:22:14.134 --> 00:22:19.126
Compared to each other they're
other, but they're all fowls.

00:22:19.126 --> 00:22:21.730
Is this a picture of same things

00:22:21.730 --> 00:22:25.780
or is this a picture of different things?

00:22:25.780 --> 00:22:28.670
Depends on what you compare it to.

00:22:28.670 --> 00:22:33.187
Anyway, I thought it was a cute example.

00:22:33.187 --> 00:22:38.144
All right, let's keep going here.

00:22:38.144 --> 00:22:41.818
,DE NI DE DANG PHRAD PA MED,

00:22:41.818 --> 00:22:45.417
,GZHAN DANG GZHAN YANG PHRAD MI 'GYUR

00:22:45.417 --> 00:22:48.500
When you talk about two
things making contact,

00:22:48.500 --> 00:22:53.075
is it that one thing
makes contact with itself?

00:22:53.075 --> 00:22:57.429
Can Rebecca make contact with Rebecca?

00:22:57.429 --> 00:23:00.320
No, cannot, right?

00:23:00.320 --> 00:23:02.270
We're talking about Michael seeing,

00:23:02.270 --> 00:23:04.970
act of seeing, Rebecca
over there being seen.

00:23:04.970 --> 00:23:09.907
Can, by herself, can Rebecca
make contact with Rebecca?

00:23:09.907 --> 00:23:13.690
No, cannot, because she's the same thing.

00:23:13.690 --> 00:23:15.344
They got to be different to make contact.

00:23:15.344 --> 00:23:17.010
GZHAN DANG GZHAN YANG PHRAD MI 'GYUR

00:23:17.010 --> 00:23:19.440
Things that are, a thing which is itself

00:23:19.440 --> 00:23:21.060
cannot make contact with itself,

00:23:21.060 --> 00:23:22.985
and a thing which is different

00:23:22.985 --> 00:23:26.293
can't make contact with
something else either.

00:23:26.293 --> 00:23:27.870
That's the verse.

00:23:27.870 --> 00:23:30.767
The first half is easy.

00:23:30.767 --> 00:23:34.893
Rebecca can't contact herself,

00:23:34.893 --> 00:23:39.156
but neither can she contact Geshe-la,

00:23:39.156 --> 00:23:40.800
who is different. Why?

00:23:41.890 --> 00:23:45.350
If they were different, they
couldn't really make contact

00:23:45.350 --> 00:23:49.408
because there can't be a point of sharing,

00:23:49.408 --> 00:23:53.668
because at that point of
sharing, they would be the same.

00:23:53.668 --> 00:23:57.118
To be truly different
means no contact, ever.

00:23:57.118 --> 00:23:59.000
If we share a point of contact

00:23:59.000 --> 00:24:02.740
then we're not truly
different. We overlap somehow.

00:24:02.740 --> 00:24:03.573
Okay?

00:24:03.573 --> 00:24:06.030
It's not possible for me to touch her,

00:24:06.030 --> 00:24:09.005
to make contact. It's not possible.

00:24:09.005 --> 00:24:13.010
We think so, but that's a
seed opening in our mind.

00:24:13.010 --> 00:24:16.700
But actually the two
physical things cannot touch,

00:24:16.700 --> 00:24:20.416
not possible.

00:24:20.416 --> 00:24:23.333
And you know in mathematics it's possible

00:24:23.333 --> 00:24:26.000
because the point is theoretical.

00:24:26.000 --> 00:24:28.642
It's just an idea, there's
no width to a point.

00:24:28.642 --> 00:24:32.069
But in reality there would have to be

00:24:32.069 --> 00:24:35.232
a point of contact that had width.

00:24:35.232 --> 00:24:39.982
And then that would be a
certain kind of millimeters,

00:24:39.982 --> 00:24:43.672
but if you took half of that millimeter,

00:24:43.672 --> 00:24:47.360
could there still be contact? Like that.

00:24:47.360 --> 00:24:48.193
And you go forever.

00:24:48.193 --> 00:24:51.801
Okay, all right.

00:24:51.801 --> 00:24:55.625
Next verse.

00:24:55.625 --> 00:24:57.166
,PHRAD BZHIN PA DANG PHRAD PA DANG,

00:24:57.166 --> 00:25:00.316
,PHRAD PA PO YANG YOD MA YIN,

00:25:00.316 --> 00:25:03.978
PHRAD BZHIN PA means 'touching',

00:25:03.978 --> 00:25:06.786
the BZHIN PA, right, Tim?, I-N-G.

00:25:06.786 --> 00:25:11.737
Touching, and being in
the act of touching,

00:25:11.737 --> 00:25:16.737
the touching and the toucher, don't exist.

00:25:16.737 --> 00:25:19.945
That's Nagarjuna's next statement.

00:25:19.945 --> 00:25:22.290
I like Choney Lama's explanations.

00:25:22.290 --> 00:25:24.990
And I'm not going to
do Choney Lama with you

00:25:24.990 --> 00:25:27.220
because it would take 20 years.

00:25:27.220 --> 00:25:30.225
But in this case it's kind of sweet.

00:25:30.225 --> 00:25:34.881
So let's go read Choney Lama.

00:25:34.881 --> 00:25:37.206
PHRAD PA NGO BO NYID KYIS YOD NA

00:25:37.206 --> 00:25:40.164
If things make contact

00:25:40.164 --> 00:25:40.997
in and of themselves.

00:25:40.997 --> 00:25:44.647
CHA THAMS CAD NAS PHRAD DAM,

00:25:44.647 --> 00:25:47.855
PHYOGS GCIG PHRAD LA

00:25:47.855 --> 00:25:50.490
If two things make contact,

00:25:50.490 --> 00:25:53.862
does every part of the
two things make contact,

00:25:53.862 --> 00:25:58.070
or does only part of the
two things make contact?

00:25:58.070 --> 00:26:02.977
First, here we go, if Geshe-la
made contact with Rebecca,

00:26:02.977 --> 00:26:05.540
would it be that every part of Geshe-la

00:26:05.540 --> 00:26:07.090
makes contact with Rebecca?

00:26:07.090 --> 00:26:09.950
Or just some parts of Geshe-la
make contact with Rebecca?

00:26:09.950 --> 00:26:11.510
Which one?

00:26:11.510 --> 00:26:12.930
The second one, because I can't...

00:26:12.930 --> 00:26:14.720
if all the parts of me make contact

00:26:14.720 --> 00:26:17.500
with all the parts of her,
I'd be inside her body,

00:26:17.500 --> 00:26:22.240
we'd be exactly the same
height, and like that.

00:26:22.240 --> 00:26:24.950
So, you know, it's
natural to say, "Geshe-la,

00:26:24.950 --> 00:26:27.270
if you ever make contact with Rebecca,

00:26:27.270 --> 00:26:29.647
like you do this elbow thing,

00:26:29.647 --> 00:26:32.200
then it's only the tip of your elbow

00:26:32.200 --> 00:26:33.691
and the tip of her elbow."

00:26:33.691 --> 00:26:38.165
PHYOGS GCIG MA PHRAD PA GANG YIN (Busted)

00:26:38.165 --> 00:26:43.165
DANG PO LTAR NA CHA THAMS
CAD NAS THAMS CAD DU

00:26:43.165 --> 00:26:45.523
GCIG CING 'DRES PAR 'GYUR

00:26:45.523 --> 00:26:48.022
If it's that every part of Geshe-la

00:26:48.022 --> 00:26:49.820
makes contact with every part of Rebecca

00:26:49.820 --> 00:26:53.370
then they would be mixed
together inseparably.

00:26:53.370 --> 00:26:54.820
PHYI MA LTAR NA

00:26:54.820 --> 00:26:57.580
Now if it's just part
of Geshe-la that touches

00:26:57.580 --> 00:26:59.680
just part of Rebecca,

00:26:59.680 --> 00:27:02.588
PHYI MA LTAR NA NGO BO NYID
KYIS PHRAD PA 'GAL BAS,

00:27:02.588 --> 00:27:05.559
PHRAD BZHIN PA DANG PHRAD ZIN PA
DANG PHRAD PA PO RNAMS NGO BOS

00:27:05.559 --> 00:27:08.167
GRUB PA YANG YOD PA MA YIN NO,,

00:27:08.167 --> 00:27:10.859
NGO BO NYID KYIS PHRAD PA 'GAL BAS

00:27:10.859 --> 00:27:13.605
If you're saying that it's
just one part of Geshe-la

00:27:13.605 --> 00:27:17.337
that makes contact with Rebecca,

00:27:17.337 --> 00:27:22.160
then the idea of contact is destroyed.

00:27:22.160 --> 00:27:23.330
Why?

00:27:23.330 --> 00:27:26.860
Because then there
would have to be a point

00:27:26.860 --> 00:27:28.859
where we were the same.

00:27:28.859 --> 00:27:32.160
Some part of Michael would
have to be part of Rebecca

00:27:32.160 --> 00:27:35.088
if there was contact.

00:27:35.088 --> 00:27:39.779
And then it wouldn't be two
different people making contact.

00:27:39.779 --> 00:27:42.002
PHRAD BZHIN PA DANG PHRAD ZIN PA

00:27:42.002 --> 00:27:44.520
He clarifies the root text by saying

00:27:44.520 --> 00:27:45.353
PHRAD ZIN PA

00:27:45.353 --> 00:27:46.790
for the second PHRAD

00:27:46.790 --> 00:27:48.450
The first PHRAD is okay,

00:27:48.450 --> 00:27:51.310
'touching', and then our author

00:27:51.310 --> 00:27:55.090
adds E-D to the second, 'touched'.

00:27:55.090 --> 00:28:00.030
And then, the toucher cannot
exist in and of themselves.

00:28:00.030 --> 00:28:03.070
If they did they couldn't touch.

00:28:03.070 --> 00:28:07.720
Now the part I like, why
I'm reading you Choney Lama,

00:28:07.720 --> 00:28:11.360
is his last statement here,
which is very helpful.

00:28:11.360 --> 00:28:13.504
Because we need help, right?

00:28:13.504 --> 00:28:17.362
RANG LUGS NI, THA SNYAD DU
MA BU DANG ME SHING DANG

00:28:17.362 --> 00:28:21.145
'O CHU SOGS LA PHRAD PA'I
CHA YOD PAR 'DOD KYANG,

00:28:21.145 --> 00:28:23.280
Look, so Nagarjuna,

00:28:23.280 --> 00:28:24.441
what's your RANG LUGS?

00:28:24.441 --> 00:28:25.900
What's that mean?

00:28:25.900 --> 00:28:28.425
Tim, what's RANG LUGS?

00:28:28.425 --> 00:28:30.150
Yes, what's your position, Nagarjuna?

00:28:30.150 --> 00:28:31.720
You know, you've been like just saying

00:28:31.720 --> 00:28:34.010
a 1,000 times what's wrong.

00:28:34.010 --> 00:28:35.660
Can you tell us what your position is?

00:28:35.660 --> 00:28:38.075
Which he does not do.

00:28:38.075 --> 00:28:40.935
It's not his habit.

00:28:40.935 --> 00:28:44.308
But, so Choney Lama
puts words in his mouth.

00:28:44.308 --> 00:28:48.376
He says, THA SNYAD DU

00:28:48.376 --> 00:28:52.673
Nominally, in words only, yes,

00:28:52.673 --> 00:28:56.389
a mother can touch her child,

00:28:56.389 --> 00:28:59.030
fire can touch firewood,

00:28:59.030 --> 00:29:03.240
and you can mix milk and water together.

00:29:03.240 --> 00:29:04.930
By the way, the image of milk,

00:29:04.930 --> 00:29:07.631
mixing milk and water together
is famous in Buddhism.

00:29:07.631 --> 00:29:10.181
Do you remember why?

00:29:10.181 --> 00:29:12.770
[student responding indistinctly]

00:29:12.770 --> 00:29:17.702
Yes, dividing ultimate
reality from relative reality.

00:29:17.702 --> 00:29:21.610
And they say there's a
tradition in ancient Asia

00:29:21.610 --> 00:29:25.480
that ducks, if you mix
water and milk together

00:29:25.480 --> 00:29:28.410
in a glass and offer it
to a goose or a duck,

00:29:28.410 --> 00:29:32.181
they can drink the milk
and leave the water.

00:29:32.181 --> 00:29:34.320
So they say that's easier

00:29:34.320 --> 00:29:38.900
than picking emptiness out
of relative reality [Laughs].

00:29:38.900 --> 00:29:42.400
So anyway, can you mix water and milk?

00:29:42.400 --> 00:29:46.830
Can you, can a fire burn a piece of wood?

00:29:46.830 --> 00:29:49.062
Can a mother touch her child?

00:29:49.062 --> 00:29:51.680
We say is there a PHRAD PA'I CHA,

00:29:51.680 --> 00:29:53.700
is there a point of contact?

00:29:53.700 --> 00:29:56.750
And we say YOD 'DOD 'DOD

00:29:56.750 --> 00:29:58.620
Now I'm Nagarjuna, 'DOD,

00:29:58.620 --> 00:30:00.907
but only THA SNYAD DU,

00:30:00.907 --> 00:30:02.650
only nominally, only in words.

00:30:02.650 --> 00:30:05.003
What's it mean, only in words?

00:30:05.003 --> 00:30:05.836
MING @DE SHAG MTSAMS

00:30:05.836 --> 00:30:08.650
MING @DE SHAG MTSAMS

00:30:08.650 --> 00:30:10.430
Words doesn't mean words here,

00:30:10.430 --> 00:30:14.210
words means mental pictures.

00:30:14.210 --> 00:30:17.300
In pictures, the pictures
can meet, that's okay.

00:30:17.300 --> 00:30:19.320
The pictures can meet, but in reality,

00:30:19.320 --> 00:30:23.635
outside, they never meet.

00:30:23.635 --> 00:30:26.210
Now, here he nails it down, okay,

00:30:26.210 --> 00:30:28.493
Choney Lama, yay Choney Lama.

00:30:28.493 --> 00:30:29.852
PHRAD PA'I TSUL

00:30:29.852 --> 00:30:33.156
You want to know how they make contact?

00:30:33.156 --> 00:30:35.710
DON DAM DPYOD BYED KYI
RIGS PAS DPYAD PA'I TSE

00:30:35.710 --> 00:30:38.126
If you really dig into it,

00:30:38.126 --> 00:30:41.626
MI RNYED

00:30:41.626 --> 00:30:44.100
You cannot find it.

00:30:44.100 --> 00:30:49.100
If you just relax and
shake Rebecca's hands,

00:30:49.350 --> 00:30:52.100
okay that's fine, you touched her.

00:30:52.100 --> 00:30:56.560
Leave it at that.

00:30:56.560 --> 00:30:59.935
What's that called?

00:30:59.935 --> 00:31:01.205
@BDAG MIN

00:31:01.205 --> 00:31:03.930
Don't dig, don't dig into it.

00:31:03.930 --> 00:31:05.370
You want to shake her
hand, shake her hand.

00:31:05.370 --> 00:31:09.032
Okay, shake hands. Make a contract, yay!

00:31:09.032 --> 00:31:11.493
Now, but if you really dig into it,

00:31:11.493 --> 00:31:13.260
you never shook hands,

00:31:13.260 --> 00:31:15.493
therefore the contract
doesn't hold, right?

00:31:15.493 --> 00:31:17.720
(student laughing)
Something like that (laughs).

00:31:17.720 --> 00:31:19.572
So if you really dig into it,

00:31:19.572 --> 00:31:23.018
@MA BDAG MA DPYAD PAR means

00:31:23.018 --> 00:31:25.880
'if you just go through
your everyday life',

00:31:25.880 --> 00:31:28.220
say your Medicine Buddha mantras,

00:31:28.220 --> 00:31:31.310
you know, somebody gets
helped, that's okay.

00:31:31.310 --> 00:31:33.060
Don't dig too deep.

00:31:33.060 --> 00:31:35.230
But if you really look into it,

00:31:35.230 --> 00:31:38.038
the mantra never touches the cancer.

00:31:38.038 --> 00:31:40.851
So what's really going on?

00:31:40.851 --> 00:31:45.653
That's if you ask beyond the pictures.

00:31:45.653 --> 00:31:48.580
If you stay in the realm of
the pictures everything's okay.

00:31:48.580 --> 00:31:49.950
Makes sense.

00:31:49.950 --> 00:31:54.573
If you try to explain it
without mental pictures,

00:31:54.573 --> 00:31:56.760
the mantra can't work.

00:31:56.760 --> 00:31:59.693
Cool?

00:31:59.693 --> 00:32:01.633
We finished the chapter, yay!

00:32:01.633 --> 00:32:03.200
We finished the chapter on sansarga.

00:32:03.200 --> 00:32:04.940
What's that mean, sansarga?

00:32:04.940 --> 00:32:06.512
Not Sansara.

00:32:06.512 --> 00:32:07.345
- [Student] Coming together.

00:32:07.345 --> 00:32:10.390
- Yes, coming together and making contact.

00:32:10.390 --> 00:32:13.020
You can make contact with other things,

00:32:13.020 --> 00:32:16.930
but it's only happening
through mental images

00:32:16.930 --> 00:32:18.607
and not really outside.

00:32:18.607 --> 00:32:20.720
The picture I had for that last one,

00:32:20.720 --> 00:32:25.500
by the way, was an intersection.

00:32:25.500 --> 00:32:28.620
And is it possible that somehow

00:32:28.620 --> 00:32:30.820
Geshe-la intersects with Rebecca?

00:32:30.820 --> 00:32:35.692
Yes, if you don't look too close.

00:32:35.692 --> 00:32:38.653
All right, see you guys
in the next chapter.

